  "body": "Parent: [#6019](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/6019) (semi-automated ingestion operations). Research source: prior-art doc `~/workspace/scratch/atlas-ingestion-brief-2026-11-04/prior-art-research.md` (2026-11-04). Follow-up 19 (Cluster 3). Provenance substrate: #3125.\n\n## Finding (research, in substance)\n\nin-toto / SLSA show how to bind a claim to content: an attestation = envelope + **subject** (artifacts by digest) + **predicate** (typed claim); SLSA's predicate carries builder identity, build parameters, and **materials** (input artifacts with digests). Translated to ingestion, each batch gets an attestation-shaped record:\n\n- **subject** = the chunk/span hashes written;\n- **materials** = the source files' hashes + source marks (sibling grammar design under #6018);\n- **builder** = ingester name + version (+ git hash, per the fleet's versioning ruling);\n- **predicate extras** = classification tier + scan results (classification design family under #6018).\n\nSigning is optional for a personal system; the *shape* is the value — \"where did this embed come from\" becomes a record lookup, not archaeology.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Record schema + where it lives (beside the staging/publish gate, sibling under #6019); one attestation per batch, covering publish and rejection outcomes.\n- How attestations chain: a re-ingest of the same source references the prior batch's attestation.\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA record schema design + emission points in the ingest pipeline.\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=muse state=filed source=main-chat-2026-11-04-wave2 -->",
